id: SECRETS-011
title: GitLab Personal Access Token
category: secrets
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .ts .tsx .js .jsx .py .java .go .rb .rs .cpp .h .cs .php .env .yml .yaml .json .toml .xml .properties .cfg .ini .conf .sh .tf .hcl
  exclude_paths: test/ vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/ __pycache__/ .venv/ target/
patterns:
  - regex: glpat-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}
    message: GitLab personal access token detected. This grants API access to GitLab on behalf of a user.
fix: Revoke the token at GitLab > User Settings > Access Tokens. Create a new token with minimal scopes and store it in CI/CD variables or a secrets manager.
